            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is \"State\" and not \"Inventory\".   Please move the file accordingly.\n\nThe reason is that we want to limit signals emitted from the Inventory interfaces."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "> The reason is that we want to limit signals emitted from the Inventory interfaces.\n\nCan you explain a bit more on this ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "abiasojo",
                        "email": "abiola.asojo@ibm.com",
                        "username": "abiasojo"
                    },
                    "message": "Patrick, I have updated to move from Inventory to state. \nThere is still a pending question from Manoj."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Can I get a reference here to where a proposed implementation of this is?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "ReadyToRemove was added to Redfish in 2025.3 for the BMC, Redfish assembly, and Redfish Chassis (It was already in Drive and PCIeDevice)\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/84402/2/redfish-core/schema/dmtf/csdl/Manager_v1.xml\n\nIBM plans to use ReadyToRemove for redundant BMCs with the backend implemented most likely in the proposed BMC App  \nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/70233\n\nThis ReadyToRemove is part of IBM's Concurrent maintenance \n\nI do know ReadyToRemove is used by other Redfish implementations today on PCIeDevice and Drive, although I haven't seen anything in Redfish \nhttps://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aopenbmc%2Fbmcweb%20ReadyToRemove&type=code\nhttps://github.com/ODIM-Project/ODIM/blob/81c02da794c25446817e363da87956d18b0c28dd/lib-dmtf/model/storage.go#L201"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "The way this reads, something in the system would prepare the FRU to be removed and then set this to true.  Is that what the flow is?\n\nI thought it was that a Redfish request will come in to ask that a FRU be prepared for removal, and bmcweb would set this and other code would watch it and prepare it.\n\nI could just be overthinking it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "abiasojo",
                        "email": "abiola.asojo@ibm.com",
                        "username": "abiasojo"
                    },
                    "message": "The description I used is similar to the description in the Redfish property description of ReadyToRemove in the Redfish Property Guide"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "ok, yea I see this in a PCIe schema at https://www.dmtf.org/sites/default/files/standards/documents/DSP0268_2023.1.html:\n\n\n> Setting the value to true shall cause the service to perform appropriate actions to quiesce the device. A task may spawn while the device is quiescing.\n\nThough most of the redfish descriptions have the same thing you have.\n\nMaybe could you update the wording to say something similar (e.g. setting it to true will...)?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "abiasojo",
                        "email": "abiola.asojo@ibm.com",
                        "username": "abiasojo"
                    },
                    "message": "The version 1.10+ description of ReadyToRemove doesn't have the extra information. The version 1.7+ has the extra information about setting...\n1.10+ is a more recent version, so should I go with 1.10+"
                }
            ],
