            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Does this interface require other (inventory?) interfaces to be implemented by the object?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "abiasojo",
                        "email": "abiola.asojo@ibm.com",
                        "username": "abiasojo"
                    },
                    "message": "Theree are apps that will be invoked when ReadyToRemove is set to true and false, respectively which are supposed to handle the inventory updates associated with the Concurrent Maintenance process. The details of this have not been completely flushed out."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "> Does this interface require other (inventory?) interfaces to be implemented by the object?\n\nIf you want this for your BMC, you would implement inventory.item.bmc for example."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I find this a bit confusing. Does setting this to true imply the item has been quiesced and ready to be removed, or, setting this to true kicks off the quisce process? This and the previous statement seem a bit contradictory."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "abiasojo",
                        "email": "abiola.asojo@ibm.com",
                        "username": "abiasojo"
                    },
                    "message": "Setting ReadyToRemove to \"True\"  kicks off the quiesce process and conversely setting it to \"False\" begins the process of resuming activity to the part that was just replaced."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Does there need to be a default value?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "abiasojo",
                        "email": "abiola.asojo@ibm.com",
                        "username": "abiasojo"
                    },
                    "message": "I have added the default value of false"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Should the value persist across system/bmc reboots, once a user has set it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "abiasojo",
                        "email": "abiola.asojo@ibm.com",
                        "username": "abiasojo"
                    },
                    "message": "If the active BMC reboots then the value would not persist: the user would need to redo the Concurrent Maintenance operation."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/ReadyToRemove.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "I thought it would persist until an app or client changes it?? Same as other state properties. Although, booting the system / rebooting the bmc during an operation like this, seems odd."
                }
            ],
